 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "It may be that purer minds now expect\nThe gift of man's desire. Again,\nSee what with God, and with the divine,\nWhat is this little thing alone\nWhich things in men are and do abide? Where\nIs life unharmed by despair\nOr weak to love from broken healing\nAnd faith from false hope? What changeless grace\nPours into a man's heart again again,\nLike wind upon his eyes, or heat within,\nOr beauty in him or herself,\nThat shall never wear away",
